# Data of the corner-lemma certificate (generated; untrusted until checked)

Generated by `scripts/corner/gen.py` from the letter table that `scripts/corner/Dump.lean`
prints (the order of `Letter.letters` and the codes `Letter.codeN/E/S/W`). Nothing in this
file is trusted: the class tables and the masks of `𝒟_κ` are checked against their definitions
in `Three/CornerTables.lean`, and the rounds are checked by the kernel in `Three/Corner.lean`.

* `clsN`, `clsE`, `clsS`, `clsW`: the 64 colour-class masks of each side (`classMask`).
* `dMaskA`, …: the letters of `𝔸` of one thin type, without the four corner letters with
  bit `0`; `rootIdx κ`: the index of `(a, κ, A, 1, 1)` in `Letter.letters`.
* `ups κ`: the updates `(j, e, m)` of the certificate on `V_6` (sites in raster order, index
  `13 (y + 6) + (x + 6)`): replace the mask at `j` by `m`, justified by the support in
  direction `e`. They delete the dependency cone of the root in a synchronous
  arc-consistency run, round by round; the last update deletes the root.
-/

